<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Aleppo</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1924 CE · capital Aleppo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The French-created state of northern Syria around Aleppo, which existed for four years before being merged into the State of Syria.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Following the defeat of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arab-kingdom-of-syria">Arab Kingdom of Syria</a>, the French high commissioner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-gouraud">Henri Gouraud</a> created the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in September 1920. It covered northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> valley and included the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sanjak-of-alexandretta">Sanjak of Alexandretta</a>, which had a special regime.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was governed by local notables under French supervision; its first governor was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamil-pasha-al-qudsi">Kamil Pasha al-Qudsi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo's</a> merchants suffered from the new borders, which cut the city off from its Anatolian hinterland after the 1921 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ankara-1921">Treaty of Ankara</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. In 1922 the state joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-federation">Syrian Federation</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>At the end of 1924 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> merged the states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-syria">State of Syria</a>, effective January 1925, while Alexandretta kept its autonomy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-aleppo.jpg" alt="State of Aleppo" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Aleppo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1924 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aleppo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kamil Pasha al-Qudsi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Syria, Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Aleppo State</dd></dl></aside></div>
